 "capsule": "The Qarakhanid (Kara-Khanid) confederation arose among Turkic tribes - chiefly Qarluq, Chigil, and Yaghma - across Semirech'ye and Kashgaria, becoming, after the conversion attributed to Satuq Bughra Khan around 934, the first Turkic dynasty to rule as a Muslim house over settled Central Asian lands. Governed by a dual system in which a senior Arslan Khan shared authority with a junior Bughra Khan, the Qarakhanids conquered Samanid Transoxiana by 999, taking Bukhara and ending Iranian Samanid rule, and made Kashgar and Bukhara centers of Perso-Turkic Islamic scholarship. Succession disputes within the ruling lineage fractured the unified khanate, which split permanently into eastern and western branches around 1042.",
